,title,link,text,language,family
0,Languages of Mali - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Languages_of_Mali,"Mande, Senufo, and Dogon stand out among Niger–Congo because of their divergent SOV basic word order. The Gur languages are represented by Bomu on the Bani River of Mali and Burkina Faso. Fulfulde, spoken throughout West Africa, is a member of the Senegambian branch.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
1,A Grammar of Dogul Dom,"https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega+linguistics+pack/African/Niger-Congo/Dogon/Dogul+Dom,+A+Grammar+of+(Cansler)+[draft].pdf","Dogul Dom has 20 phonemic consonants, with four other segments occurring as restricted allophones of larger phonemes. In table 3.1, the categories of postalveolar and palatal have been condensed and the lateral approximant has been grouped with other oral approximants.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
2,"Full text of ""enwiki-Dogul_Dogon-20200726.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Dogul_Dogon-20200726.pdf/enwiki-Dogul_Dogon-20200726_djvu.txt,"The Dogul language, Dogul Dom, is a Dogon language spoken in Mali. It is closest to Bondum Dogon, though not enough for mutual intelligibility. Dogul Dom Region Mali. Native speakers 16,000 (1998)W. Language Niger-Congo? family. Dogon.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
3,"Dogon, Dogul Dom language resources | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/dbg,"Listing of people groups speaking Dogon, Dogul Dom. Dogon, Dogul Dom dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
4,Dogon languages - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Dogon_languages,"The evidence linking Dogon to the Niger–Congo family is mainly a few numerals and some common core vocabulary. Various theories have been proposed, placing them with Gur, Mande, or as an independent branch, the last now being the preferred approach.Dogul Dom Dogon.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
5,Ana Dogon,https://grokipedia.com/page/ana_dogon,"Ana Dogon is classified as part of the Dogon language family, which is conventionally regarded as an independent branch within the Niger-Congo phylum.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
6,Dogul Dom,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/DogulDom,"Alternate names: Dogon, Dogul-Dom, Dogulu, Dogul Dom Dogon, North Plateau Dogon, Dogul dom, Dogul-Dom Dogon. Language code: dbg. Language family: Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Dogon (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 15,700.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
7,Endangered Languages Project - Dogul Dom,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/8737,"[aka Dogon, Dogul-Dom, Dogulu].Niger-Congo, Dogon, North Plateau. Code authority. Iso 639-3.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
8,OLAC resources in and about the Dogul Dom Dogon language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/dbg,"Other known names and dialect names: Dogul Dom Dogon, Dogul-Dom.ONLINEDogon, Dogul Dom: a language of Mali. n.a. 2018. SIL International. oai:ethnologue.com:dbg. ONLINELINGUIST List Resources for Dogon, Dogul Dom.","Dogon, Dogul Dom",Niger-Congo
